+# Runbook: Deploying Kapa Provenance + HIL + Federated Starter (Quickstart)
+
+Prereqs:
+- Kubernetes cluster for demo, kubectl access, and secrets: Vault address, S3 bucket, Rekor DB creds.
+- GitHub Actions configured with OIDC trust to Vault.
+
+Deploy steps (summary):
+1. Create namespace: kubectl create ns aegis-kapa
+2. Deploy Rekor (k8s/rekor/rekor-postgres-deployment.yaml) or use managed Rekor.
+3. Deploy Vault (helm using helm/values-vault-kapa.yaml) with KMS auto-unseal or BYOK.
+4. Deploy receipt_signer configured to use Vault transit; update RECEIPT_SIGNER_URL secret in CI.
+5. Deploy pre-load webhook (services/attestation/preload_webhook.py) as a service and point Kapa serving pre-load check to it.
+6. Deploy require_hil service and HIL UI; wire MCP or notification channels as desired.
+7. Deploy federated orchestrator (services/federated/tff_orchestrator.py) as a stub for demo rounds.
+8. Configure CI secrets and run .github/workflows/ci_kapa_full.yml to produce an attestation and evidence bundle.
+9. Validate: evidence bundle attached to model; attempting to load unsigned model fails; HIL requests appear in admin UI or MCP.
+
+Testing:
+- Use curl to hit receipt_signer /sign (operator) with a demo artifact; verify attestation & Rekor entry.
+- Run CI to confirm evidence bundle generation and upload artifact exists.
+- Simulate model load request to pre-load webhook with evidence to validate acceptance.
+
+Rollback:
+- If attestation pipeline fails, temporarily disable automatic deploys, and use manual approval (HIL) to progress critical models.
+
